drumee-infra (1.2.31) stable; urgency=medium

  * Make `dpkg-reconfigure drumee-infra` actually re-render. It did not, on any
    installed host, and it is the advice eight separate messages in this postinst
    give — including every "fix it, then reconfigure" for TLS and DNS.
    .
    dpkg-reconfigure runs `postinst configure $version`. It does NOT invoke
    `postinst reconfigure`, and nothing in dpkg or debconf does; the `reconfigure)`
    arm that passed --reconfigure=1 was dead code, unreachable since it was
    written, and it looked exactly like the fix for this while being nothing of the
    kind. The reachable arm runs setup-infra's bin/install, which called
    `node infra.js` with no arguments, so hasExistingSettings() found
    /etc/drumee/drumee.json, printed "Use --reconfigure=1" and returned true. Every
    reconfigure reported success and changed not one file.
    .
    postinst now exports DRUMEE_RECONFIGURE when DEBCONF_RECONFIGURE is set —
    dpkg-reconfigure exports that itself, and running it is an explicit operator
    action whose whole purpose is to reconfigure, so it carries the intent.
    bin/install forwards it to infra.js and jitsi.js. The reconfigure_existing
    question stays as the way to ask for the same during a normal apt run, where
    re-rendering over an operator's tree must never happen on its own. The dead arm
    is gone, with a comment where it was saying why there is none.
    .
    Found by shipping 1.2.30's zone fix, running dpkg-reconfigure on the test box to
    apply it, and watching the zone file keep its original mtime. Worth stating
    plainly: 1.2.30 was correct and unreachable on any existing install.

